# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  OPTIONAL — the site works fine with NO environment variables.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The GitHub section uses the public GitHub API, which allows
# 60 requests per hour per IP. Responses are cached for 1 hour on the
# server, so a normal amount of traffic never gets close to that limit.
#
# Only add a token if you start seeing the "rate limit" message:
#
#   1. github.com -> Settings -> Developer settings
#      -> Personal access tokens -> Fine-grained tokens
#   2. Create a token with NO extra permissions (public read is enough)
#   3. Locally: copy this file to `.env.local` and paste the token below
#   4. On Vercel: Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables
#      Name: GITHUB_TOKEN   Value: <your token>   (all environments)
#
# Note there is no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — this is read on the server only
# and is never sent to the browser.

# GITHUB_TOKEN=
